Should we consider something like this? This would make it so scripts that have errors would reflect that in the documentation. I think this could be useful in the case of, e.g. plugins that have errors because they need to be updated. It's not the user's code, and the errors are likely to only show up on editor open/project start, so they are harder to track down. At least this way users can notice the errors while looking at their plugin's documentation?

